WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:56.550
<b>Foul Play</b>

3
00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:55.880
Luffy!

4
00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.560
Luffy! Luffy! Luffy!
Luffy! Luffy! Luffy!

5
00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.720
Luffy!

6
00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.030
I have terrible news:
A dinosaur ate Nami!

7
00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.130
What? No way!

8
00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:13.630
We were running through
the jungle to get away

9
00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:15.570
from the dinosaur, and then
suddenly, I turned around

10
00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.400
and she was gone!
It must've gotten her!

11
00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:21.140
I got my friend killed!

12
00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.470
How can I live with myself now?!

13
00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:27.300
Hey, you guys, calm down.

14
00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.500
Just listen to me for
a second, will you?!

15
00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.040
If she was there one
moment and gone the next,

16
00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.730
then... you can't know
for sure what happened.

17
00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.860
Well, no, it's not like
I could stop and check!

18
00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:38.920
I would've been eaten, too!

19
00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.100
It was either a dinosaur
or some other wild beast.

20
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.810
What else could it possibly be?!

21
00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.940
I don't know for sure.

22
00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.860
But, if Baroque Works followed
us from Whiskey Peak,

23
00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:49.900
it would make sense for
them to capture Nami,

24
00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.870
and not you. I think we
may be in great danger.

25
00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:54.090
We should go.

26
00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.120
You mean
that Baroque Works

27
00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:59.120
is here on the island with us?!

28
00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.900
Wait. But why capture
Nami and not me.

29
00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.930
Because you haven't
gotten in their way.

30
00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:08.600
Most likely, you aren't
on their assassination list.

31
00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.970
Oh, okay.

32
00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:11.210
Now that I think about it...

33
00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:14.950
I bet that booby-trapped alcohol
was meant to get us instead.

34
00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:17.620
Huh? What did you
say about alcohol?

35
00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.550
Brogy gave Dorry
some of your alcohol

36
00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.120
that must have
been tampered with.

37
00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:25.490
Because, when Dorry drank
the barrels, they exploded.

38
00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:27.820
No way!

39
00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:30.590
They actually exploded
inside the guy?!

40
00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:32.170
Wait! He was injured that badly,

41
00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.920
and he still ran
off to go fight?

42
00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:35.410
I tried to stop him, and that's

43
00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:37.330
how I ended up like this.

44
00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:41.430
This is horrible.

45
00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:43.270
Those two have been
fighting as hard as they can

46
00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:47.970
for 100 years! And they
always ended in a draw.

47
00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:55.140
Their duels are fought with
the most honor and pride

48
00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:56.290
in the whole world!

49
00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:56.920
Yeah.

50
00:03:56.990 --> 00:03:57.690
There's no way
they can settle it

51
00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.080
once and for all like this!

52
00:03:59.080 --> 00:03:59.780
Plus...

53
00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.270
What's... wrong... huh?

54
00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.880
Well, he keeps fighting.

55
00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.350
He certainly is stubborn...

56
00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:23.360
That Dorry the Blue Ogre.

57
00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:26.020
Yes. Well...

58
00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:28.290
I should lend some assistance.

59
00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.180
A whole century.

60
00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:49.050
This has been a long
and difficult battle, indeed.

61
00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:31.540
I now know that
this was a judgment.

62
00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:35.010
A judgment from Elbaph...
The god of war.

63
00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:39.210
I didn't have the god's
protection... and that is all.

64
00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:47.020
Stop it, Luffy.

65
00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:47.920
Calm down.

66
00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:51.620
Who was it?!

67
00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:56.290
Who did this?!

68
00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:04.680
Huh?

69
00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:06.760
Hey, Mr. 3.

70
00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:08.080
I think I heard something.

71
00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:12.220
Some pathetic
animal yelping helplessly

72
00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:15.000
in the jungle. Amusing.

73
00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:22.440
Seventy-three thousand

74
00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:30.200
four hundred sixty-seven duels.

75
00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.160
four hundred sixty-six
draws... and...

76
00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.710
Seventy-three thousand

77
00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:42.720
...one win!

78
00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.710
Do I see tears of joy?

79
00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:03.080
I doubt that happiness
will last long.

80
00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:07.290
But... For now, I offer
you my congratulations.

81
00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.090
Did you say "happiness"?

82
00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:11.360
You... know nothing.

83
00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:13.090
Who are you, little man?

84
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.710
I am Mr. 3...

85
00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:16.340
That's a codename, of course,

86
00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:18.230
which is necessary
in my line of work.

87
00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:20.830
I am an artist of sorts,
and this is my assistant.

88
00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:23.200
All the best artists
require assistants, you see.

89
00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.100
Her name is Miss Golden Week.

90
00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.800
I tell you all this
because I've already

91
00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.130
caught you in one
of my art works.

92
00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:33.900
What... What have
you done to me?!

93
00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.110
Right, Luffy!

94
00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:43.830
I don't know what
we're dealing with here,

95
00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:46.470
but I'm gonna take
care of them myself!

96
00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:47.800
I'll come, too, Usopp.

97
00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:48.800
Good.

98
00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.470
Having you along with me
will be reassuring.

99
00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:52.170
You're not goin' anywhere.

100
00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:52.870
– Huh?
– Huh?

101
00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:56.830
You guys again!

102
00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:06.170
You can have 'im back.

103
00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.170
We don't need him.

104
00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:10.840
Karoo!

105
00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:13.010
Why, you...! Wait.

106
00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:14.210
Who are these guys?

107
00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:15.980
The bullies from
the last island.

108
00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.060
Karoo never did anything to you!

109
00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:20.160
Why did you have
to do this to him?!

110
00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:21.400
You're right.

111
00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:24.980
We had no need to retaliate
against your ugly bird... but...

112
00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:26.710
We needed to get our
hands on that little

113
00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:29.820
straw hat friend
of yours, you see.

114
00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:31.020
The plan was simple.

115
00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:32.760
We wanted to lure you
both into the jungle

116
00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:36.990
by having your dear birdie here
squawk pitifully for help.

117
00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:40.060
But the idiot
refused to cooperate.

118
00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:41.060
Now...

119
00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.100
You just call out for
your owner real loud.

120
00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:47.830
Give us a really loud squawk
and we might even let you go.

121
00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:52.030
All right...

122
00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:54.360
Then we'll make you squawk.

123
00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:56.220
Just call for the princess.

124
00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:01.730
Call for help now!

125
00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:02.990
Let's hear it, bird!

126
00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:06.790
Call out to your beloved
princess and this will all end!

127
00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:09.490
Just open your mouth,
you damn creature!

128
00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:12.940
But then we realized
that little Straw Hat

129
00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:15.910
was already neatly trapped here,
just waitin' for us.

130
00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:16.780
In which case...

131
00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:19.120
...we didn't need
that thing anymore.

132
00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:20.460
Karoo...

133
00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:28.170
What a dumb bird.

134
00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:31.210
I'll kill you!

135
00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.910
And were you the ones
who planted a bomb

136
00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:36.160
to injure the giant Dorry?

137
00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:37.760
Yeah. That's us.

138
00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:40.180
Who is this new guy?
Is he on the list?

139
00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:42.250
No, but he's clearly
a friend of theirs.

140
00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:43.950
Let's just get rid of him.

141
00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:46.960
How dare you interfere
with a proud warrior duel?!

142
00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:50.520
It was you?! I'll
kick your... asses!

143
00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.120
How about I get
rid of you instead!

144
00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.230
Aw... It's just so cute when
you fight, Miss Wednesday.

145
00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:59.370
What's more,

146
00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.030
she really thinks
she stands a chance

147
00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.360
against agents like us.

148
00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:04.460
Taste my Peacock Slasher!

149
00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:05.830
I'll get you, too!

150
00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.530
Exploding Star!

151
00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:11.470
Yeah, got ya!

152
00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.140
Wrong!

153
00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:16.810
Huh?

154
00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:18.740
Nose Fancy Cannon!

155
00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:25.710
Did you get burned?

156
00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:27.440
Usopp!

157
00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:31.110
Ten Thousand Kilogram Press!

158
00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:33.310
Now, now.

159
00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.380
– Just calm down.

160
00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:44.230
There's no need to get so upset

161
00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:45.000
right now, Princess.

162
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.220
We aren't plannin'
to kill you yet.

163
00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.840
We only came here to abduct you.

164
00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.670
Those were Mr. 3's
explicit orders.

165
00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:01.780
Mr. 3? The Wax-Wax Fruit man?

166
00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:03.750
He's here on the island with us?

167
00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:04.850
That's right.

168
00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.950
Mr. 3 the "candle man."

169
00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:11.120
His body creates wax, which he
can then control as he likes.

170
00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:17.590
What's going on here? Tell me!

171
00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:24.770
Going on? Of course it's
lost on someone like you.

172
00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:26.150
What's going on
is that I'm creating

173
00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:28.570
a work of art
with your assistance.

174
00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:36.580
Stand still
like a good little girl.

175
00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:38.880
Did you actually think
that someone like you could

176
00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:42.080
escape from an organization
like Baroque Works?

177
00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:49.370
After all, your
friend over there

178
00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.050
has a big bounty on his head,

179
00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:53.160
and look at what
happened to him.

180
00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:55.720
Consider this
our "thank you"

181
00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:57.690
for what happened
at Whiskey Peak.

182
00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:58.870
You should learn to mind

183
00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:00.930
your own business, you pathetic
group of wannabe pirates.

184
00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:03.000
It would be quite
beneficial to your health.

185
00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.990
By the way, we have
your swordsman friend.

186
00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:06.140
And we've captured
the other girl

187
00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:08.860
that you brought
along with you as well.

188
00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:10.610
So you caught... Zoro?

189
00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:11.560
Damn right.

190
00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:14.060
In that case, you're
in more trouble than I thought.

191
00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:16.070
Well...

192
00:12:16.070 --> 00:12:18.040
Let's see how big you talk...

193
00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.970
...after one of my
Kicky Bombs blows up

194
00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:21.070
that little face of yours.

195
00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:23.810
Try whatever tricks you want.

196
00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:25.580
I'm gonna kick your ass.

197
00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:31.250
This should be fun.

198
00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:35.400
Luffy, no!

199
00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:39.660
Die!

200
00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:53.220
You weak little fool.

201
00:12:53.420 --> 00:12:55.050
Luffy!

202
00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:56.690
No... please...

203
00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:57.460
Luffy! Get up!

204
00:12:57.720 --> 00:12:59.300
Let's go, Miss Valentine.

205
00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:03.470
Usopp! Karoo!

206
00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:25.580
Damn you!

207
00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.410
Struggling is pointless.

208
00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:30.640
Once my candle jacket
solidifies around you,

209
00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:32.810
it'll become as hard as
iron, and it's impossible

210
00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:33.880
to break through.

211
00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:36.940
There's no denying
that you giants

212
00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:39.550
are very strong. But once
you've been captured,

213
00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:41.820
that strength doesn't
do you any good at all.

214
00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:42.750
None.

215
00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:44.750
All that I had to do
was use my brain.

216
00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:46.480
There would be no sense
in trying to defeat you

217
00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:48.750
in a physical fight.

218
00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:51.510
You were so busy
enjoying your great win

219
00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.860
that capturing you was easy.

220
00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:57.030
Don't glare at me like that!

221
00:13:57.030 --> 00:14:00.120
It's positively terrifying.

222
00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:02.460
You should be celebrating,
shouldn't you?

223
00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:05.080
At long last, your battle
with Dorry the Blue Ogre

224
00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:06.720
has come to an end.

225
00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:08.510
You fought on this
island for 100 years

226
00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:09.990
for your precious pride.

227
00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:12.550
Shouldn't such a long lasting
battle make victory

228
00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:13.860
all the more sweet?

229
00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:16.630
I mean really,
it's an accomplishment!

230
00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:19.570
Even if it required
a little outside help.

231
00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:21.510
Come on, give me
a little smile.

232
00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:24.540
Shut up! What would
you know about this?

233
00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:30.010
Of course, the real
victor in all of this is...

234
00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:30.790
...me.

235
00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.970
The bounties placed
on your heads long ago

236
00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.940
remain in place to this day.

237
00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:40.110
Today you're worth
200,000,000 berries.

238
00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:41.970
Quite a handsome sum.

239
00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:43.260
Bounties?

240
00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:44.330
Big bounties.

241
00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:47.930
I feel as if I've uncovered
a long-lost treasure.

242
00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:49.910
So that's what
you're after here!

243
00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:52.000
Mr. 3...

244
00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.450
Here's the girl.

245
00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:56.690
Alabasta's sneaky spy.

246
00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:57.920
It's about time.

247
00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.500
I was positively
sick of waiting.

248
00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.690
You're full of nothing
but dirty tricks!

249
00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:02.890
I can't believe you!

250
00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:06.190
Putting a bomb in Dorry's
alcohol was low, even for you!

251
00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:06.890
What?!

252
00:15:06.890 --> 00:15:07.700
Uh...

253
00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.450
The barrels?

254
00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:12.740
You did something to the
drinks that I gave Dorry?

255
00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:16.550
Dorry, how was your drink?

256
00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:18.690
Hit the spot, didn't it?

257
00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:20.060
Yes.

258
00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.560
It tasted almost
godly in fact.

259
00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:26.330
No! That must
be what Dorry meant...

260
00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:28.640
Hm. You're an
annoying little girl, Princess...

261
00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:30.670
giving away our
secrets like that.

262
00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:31.740
But that's all right.

263
00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:35.010
There isn't anything he
can do about it now anyway.

264
00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:39.700
Candle...

265
00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:40.970
...Lock!

266
00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:49.840
Mr. 5!

267
00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:53.040
Bring the swordsman
and the other girl.

268
00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:55.960
Time to begin.

269
00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:10.200
Giant... Candle... Set!

270
00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.250
What is that thing?

271
00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:33.720
Here are the others.

272
00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:40.200
It's just sad.

273
00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:43.300
Idiots like these shoulda been

274
00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:45.710
a lot easier for me to catch.

275
00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:47.140
Shoulda caught 'em
the first time.

276
00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:47.990
How embarrassin'.

277
00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:49.610
What is that thing?!

278
00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:52.150
Nothing good.
I'm sorry, you guys!

279
00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:53.720
But... Vivi...

280
00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:55.720
What happened? I thought
you were with Luffy!

281
00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:57.800
I was... but now...

282
00:16:57.800 --> 00:16:59.900
If you're wonderin'
about the Straw Hat,

283
00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:02.970
I saw to that
little runt myself.

284
00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:05.800
He didn't put up
much of a fight either.

285
00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:07.410
Yeah, right.

286
00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:26.000
Welcome, one and all,

287
00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:28.910
to my famous candle service set.

288
00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:33.330
I guess this is
what it feels like

289
00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:35.270
to be a candle stuck
on a birthday cake.

290
00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:38.910
What's that spinning up there?

291
00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:42.770
I can't move. Great.

292
00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:43.940
It's not surprising to me that

293
00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:46.110
they don't want
us moving around.

294
00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:48.240
That's what "captured" means.

295
00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:53.780
Damn... That stuff's hard.

296
00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:55.680
And I can't put much
strength behind my swing

297
00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:57.620
from this angle.

298
00:17:57.620 --> 00:17:58.620
Something's falling.

299
00:17:58.620 --> 00:18:04.280
I do hope you
enjoy my candle service.

300
00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:05.900
You may have noticed
the wax flakes

301
00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.120
that are falling from above.

302
00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:10.790
You'll eventually be covered
and turned into wax figures.

303
00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:14.090
You'll become perfectly lifelike
statues for my collection.

304
00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:17.290
Something that even I
couldn't achieve on my own.

305
00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:18.920
I will literally
capture your spirits

306
00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:22.240
and encase them
forever in wax shells.

307
00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:24.400
It will be a true masterpiece.

308
00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:27.890
You will die for my art.

309
00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:29.740
I don't think so, you freak!

310
00:18:29.740 --> 00:18:31.760
I have no interest in
dying for whatever it is

311
00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:33.240
you consider art!

312
00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:34.140
Hey, giant!

313
00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:35.380
Why are you laying
there doing nothing

314
00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:39.150
when you could be beating the
crap out of this candle guy?

315
00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:42.230
Now he is gonna make
one huge statue.

316
00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:44.310
Heh! You can
try to convince him,

317
00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:46.260
but your efforts
will be useless.

318
00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:48.000
He's a little blue
at the moment.

319
00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:50.900
You see, he just realized how
unfairly he won his last fight,

320
00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:53.070
and he's lost the
heart to celebrate.

321
00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:54.690
He killed his dear friend Dorry,

322
00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:57.010
with whom he had
fought for 100 years.

323
00:18:57.010 --> 00:18:59.810
Dorry was injured.
But he didn't notice.

324
00:18:59.810 --> 00:19:00.860
Just imagine how much pain

325
00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:04.410
Dorry must have been in.
He didn't stand a chance.

326
00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.240
You did shed
a few tears, though.

327
00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:08.170
Perhaps you were crying
for your friend?

328
00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:11.840
Now it's no use.
There's no undoing it.

329
00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:14.180
He's dead! And it's
all your fault!

330
00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:26.380
I should have seen it.

331
00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:29.680
I knew something
strange was going on.

332
00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:36.860
From the moment
we first began to fight,

333
00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:38.390
I knew Dorry was
hiding something,

334
00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:41.330
but I couldn't tell what it was.

335
00:19:41.330 --> 00:19:43.400
You say that you knew it?

336
00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:44.660
You're lying!

337
00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:47.770
If you knew something was wrong,
why didn't you stop the fight?

338
00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:49.920
Why didn't you give him
a chance to rest?

339
00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:52.230
I didn't see one shred of pity
in the way you ruthlessly

340
00:19:52.270 --> 00:19:53.660
cut him down.

341
00:19:56.240 --> 00:19:58.480
You know nothing
about honorable duels!

342
00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:03.380
Someone like you could
never understand my tears.

343
00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:06.110
What do you know
about the way of Elbaph?

344
00:20:06.110 --> 00:20:09.120
You think that I would shame
a warrior who hid the fact

345
00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:12.750
that he was weakened so that
he could continue to fight?

346
00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:18.660
Only a truly great warrior
would go to such lengths,

347
00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:22.360
and such a man isn't
interested in pity!

348
00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:23.130
Huh?

349
00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:23.800
Now...

350
00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:26.630
I know what really happened.

351
00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:28.200
And I must do
something about it.

352
00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:31.300
I'm going to finish this
with my own two hands.

353
00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:41.510
That's the least
I can do for Dorry.

354
00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:45.080
He was a great warrior
and my dear friend!

355
00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:49.640
Brogy!

356
00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:58.220
– Brogy!
– Brogy!

357
00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:00.530
His chatterin' was
gettin' on my nerves.

358
00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:04.430
U... Usopp... Usopp...

359
00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:12.240
They have to... pay for this.

360
00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:17.240
Oh, yeah.
Those jerks have to pay.

361
00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:28.620
You can't... take this either?

362
00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:37.580
Heh. All right.
Then it's settled.

363
00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:40.050
Let's go beat them senseless.

364
00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:40.850
Brogy!

365
00:21:40.850 --> 00:21:43.490
Big fool!

366
00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:46.360
It seems that I miscalculated.

367
00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:49.750
I forgot how freakishly strong
these dumb giants can be.

368
00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:52.570
It looks like you're
going to require

369
00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:54.990
more complete restraints.

370
00:21:54.990 --> 00:21:58.960
Wax-Wax... Handcuffs!

371
00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:02.600
Still going!

372
00:22:08.960 --> 00:22:11.400
And now for the finishing touch.

373
00:22:11.430 --> 00:22:12.480
Take this!

374
00:22:22.210 --> 00:22:24.210
It'll be tough for you
to move now, won't it?

375
00:22:33.590 --> 00:22:35.760
You really are despicable.

376
00:22:35.760 --> 00:22:39.430
Now! Let's get these
candles going faster!

377
00:22:39.430 --> 00:22:42.250
It's time to turn these
people into beautiful,

378
00:22:42.280 --> 00:22:44.320
artistic wax statues!

379
00:22:48.260 --> 00:22:50.270
My chest is starting to hurt.

380
00:22:50.270 --> 00:22:52.480
The wax is starting
to get into our lungs.

381
00:22:52.480 --> 00:22:55.850
At this rate, he's gonna turn us
into wax from the inside out!

382
00:22:57.890 --> 00:22:58.990
That's it.

383
00:22:58.990 --> 00:23:01.160
Make it look like you're
in as much pain as possible!

384
00:23:01.160 --> 00:23:02.390
That's perfect.

385
00:23:02.390 --> 00:23:04.340
Expressions of agony
are what I seek

386
00:23:04.370 --> 00:23:05.570
to achieve in my art!

387
00:23:05.570 --> 00:23:09.170
The finished product
will be simply splendid!

388
00:23:09.170 --> 00:23:11.440
You must die filled with terror!

389
00:23:11.440 --> 00:23:13.440
This is what you
call art, you creepy,

390
00:23:13.440 --> 00:23:16.780
weird-haired freak?!
You guys are gonna regret this!

391
00:23:16.780 --> 00:23:19.380
You're gonna pay for what
you did to Brogy and Dorry

392
00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:21.220
and for what you're
trying to do to us!

393
00:23:21.220 --> 00:23:23.620
Yell and scream
all you want to, little girl.

394
00:23:23.620 --> 00:23:25.590
No one can help you now.

395
00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:34.090
A century...

396
00:23:41.930 --> 00:23:44.500
For 100 years,
Dorry and I dueled

397
00:23:44.530 --> 00:23:47.680
day in and day out,
fighting endlessly.

398
00:23:47.680 --> 00:23:49.480
We battled for our pride,

399
00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:52.020
as is the way of the
warriors of Elbaph.

400
00:23:52.020 --> 00:23:54.940
We fought with honor
and with strength.

401
00:23:54.940 --> 00:23:57.440
And still, we are
subjected to this.

402
00:23:57.440 --> 00:23:59.810
Why has this happened to us?!

403
00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:03.680
Must we be
forced to meet our end

404
00:24:03.710 --> 00:24:06.680
in such a way? Must we?

405
00:24:06.680 --> 00:24:08.750
It isn't fair for a
warrior to die such

406
00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:13.140
a dishonorable death!
Why can I not die in battle?!

407
00:24:14.680 --> 00:24:17.310
Hold that look.

408
00:24:17.310 --> 00:24:18.380
Yes, that's it.

409
00:24:18.380 --> 00:24:20.320
Such grief... Such sorrow!

410
00:24:20.320 --> 00:24:21.650
And just the right
amount of anger.

411
00:24:21.650 --> 00:24:22.720
How marvelous.

412
00:24:24.650 --> 00:24:27.790
Elbaph, please!

413
00:24:27.790 --> 00:24:29.210
This isn't good.

414
00:24:29.210 --> 00:24:30.900
My hands won't move.
Can't we do something?

415
00:24:30.900 --> 00:24:31.830
I don't wanna die like this!

416
00:24:32.160 --> 00:24:34.370
My body's already
beginning to turn stiff.

417
00:24:35.020 --> 00:24:36.950
What are we supposed to do?

418
00:24:36.950 --> 00:24:39.190
Zoro, do something!

419
00:24:39.190 --> 00:24:40.060
Hey, giant.

420
00:24:40.060 --> 00:24:40.760
Huh?

421
00:24:41.380 --> 00:24:42.880
You can still move, right?

422
00:24:43.940 --> 00:24:47.510
Good. So can I.

423
00:24:47.510 --> 00:24:49.880
I say we take 'em down together.

424
00:24:49.880 --> 00:24:50.880
What do you think?

425
00:24:52.450 --> 00:24:53.150
Hold on a second.

426
00:24:53.150 --> 00:24:55.480
What are you doing? Are you...?

427
00:24:55.480 --> 00:24:56.320
Yeah.

428
00:24:56.320 --> 00:24:57.460
Quit messing around...
your not gonna

429
00:24:57.490 --> 00:24:58.490
cut your own legs off!

430
00:24:58.490 --> 00:25:00.290
I'm not messing around at all.

431
00:25:00.290 --> 00:25:02.830
It's the only way to get us
out of this situation.

432
00:25:02.830 --> 00:25:03.660
Are you in or out?

433
00:25:03.660 --> 00:25:05.510
Are you insane? No way!

434
00:25:05.510 --> 00:25:08.500
Even if you get down from here,
you won't get far without legs!

435
00:25:08.500 --> 00:25:11.750
There's no way to
know for sure until we try.

436
00:25:11.750 --> 00:25:14.590
So are you saying you'd
rather just sit here and die?

437
00:25:14.590 --> 00:25:17.720
Why should we make it easy
for those guys to kill us?

438
00:25:17.720 --> 00:25:19.270
Dying quietly without a struggle

439
00:25:19.300 --> 00:25:21.120
doesn't make you
any less dead.

440
00:25:21.120 --> 00:25:22.530
Right?

441
00:25:22.530 --> 00:25:24.760
The girl was right.
This guy's insane.

442
00:25:24.760 --> 00:25:25.880
He's bluffing.

443
00:25:25.880 --> 00:25:28.150
There's no way he would do
something as crazy as that.

444
00:25:28.150 --> 00:25:30.190
He's just trying to act tough
so his friends will feel better.

445
00:25:33.490 --> 00:25:36.260
That runt's got spirit,
I'll give him that!

446
00:25:36.260 --> 00:25:38.190
He's doing better than I am.

447
00:25:38.190 --> 00:25:40.690
I had actually begun
to lose the will to fight.

448
00:25:40.690 --> 00:25:42.260
All right, I'm in.

449
00:25:42.260 --> 00:25:44.300
Let's cut them to pieces.

450
00:25:46.670 --> 00:25:48.770
You're not serious
about this, are you?

451
00:25:48.770 --> 00:25:50.840
How are you planning on
fighting them afterward?

452
00:25:50.840 --> 00:25:52.110
Who knows?

453
00:25:52.110 --> 00:25:55.240
But... I plan to win.

454
00:25:56.550 --> 00:25:57.790
Who are these people?!

455
00:25:57.790 --> 00:25:59.890
They're completely nuts!

456
00:26:00.370 --> 00:26:02.250
What kind of man
is he? And why...

457
00:26:03.390 --> 00:26:06.130
Why do I feel like I've seen
that look somewhere before?

458
00:26:06.130 --> 00:26:07.430
Princess Vivi!

459
00:26:08.520 --> 00:26:10.990
Sometimes it takes more
strength to live than to die.

460
00:26:10.990 --> 00:26:13.470
Wait. I'll fight with you!

461
00:26:13.470 --> 00:26:14.240
You what?

462
00:26:14.300 --> 00:26:15.640
Good. Get ready.

463
00:26:15.670 --> 00:26:19.310
And now... Let's go!

464
00:26:19.310 --> 00:26:20.240
Don't be foolish!

465
00:26:20.240 --> 00:26:21.580
What can you hope to accomplish?

466
00:26:32.160 --> 00:26:33.090
Hey!

467
00:26:33.090 --> 00:26:36.600
When I get back,
I'm gonna kick your asses!

468
00:26:39.070 --> 00:26:40.340
Huh?

469
00:26:41.960 --> 00:26:43.290
Let's get 'em, Usopp!

470
00:26:43.290 --> 00:26:43.920
Yeah!

471
00:26:44.140 --> 00:26:45.640
And bird... guy?

472
00:26:46.460 --> 00:26:47.420
Luffy! Usopp!

473
00:26:47.790 --> 00:26:48.550
Karoo!

474
00:26:48.710 --> 00:26:49.980
We're here, Brogy.

475
00:26:49.980 --> 00:26:52.710
Don't worry, we'll pick up
where you left off.

476
00:26:52.710 --> 00:26:53.590
Thanks, Usopp.

477
00:26:53.590 --> 00:26:55.540
Beat them beyond recognition!

478
00:26:55.540 --> 00:26:57.510
Show 'em "expressions
of pain and agony"

479
00:26:57.510 --> 00:26:58.820
they won't soon forget!

480
00:26:58.820 --> 00:27:00.150
Oh, I'm goin' to...

481
00:27:00.150 --> 00:27:02.250
These guys messed up
the best duel ever!

482
00:27:02.250 --> 00:27:05.590
They're in some serious trouble,
and they're gonna answer to me!

483
00:27:05.590 --> 00:27:06.820
So you're
the one with the highest

484
00:27:06.860 --> 00:27:08.590
bounty in the East Blue?

485
00:27:08.590 --> 00:27:10.660
My, how low Marine
standards have fallen.

486
00:27:10.660 --> 00:27:12.580
It's almost tragic, really.

487
00:27:12.580 --> 00:27:14.080
Is that... your hair?

488
00:27:14.080 --> 00:27:14.750
You just shut up!

489
00:27:14.750 --> 00:27:16.890
Dude it's... um... on fire...

490
00:27:16.890 --> 00:27:17.720
Hush, you!

491
00:27:17.720 --> 00:27:18.930
Yes, he has weird hair.

492
00:27:18.930 --> 00:27:20.400
Now, could you
break this pillar?!

493
00:27:20.400 --> 00:27:24.170
We're about to turn
into wax statues here.

494
00:27:24.170 --> 00:27:25.830
Oh, you guys in trouble?

495
00:27:25.830 --> 00:27:27.340
No, no trouble at all.

496
00:27:27.340 --> 00:27:29.470
Wait... Zoro, your leg!

497
00:27:30.170 --> 00:27:32.130
Yeah I made it about
halfway through, I'd say.

498
00:27:32.130 --> 00:27:35.220
And how exactly is
that no trouble at all?!

499
00:27:35.470 --> 00:27:37.510
So, Luffy, what do ya think?

500
00:27:37.510 --> 00:27:40.260
Could you go ahead and take
care of this pillar for us?

501
00:27:40.260 --> 00:27:42.040
I think I've done enough.

502
00:27:42.040 --> 00:27:43.740
Yeah, no problem.

503
00:27:44.520 --> 00:27:46.270
Hah! I wouldn't be so sure!

504
00:27:46.940 --> 00:27:48.360
I don't know what it is...

505
00:27:48.390 --> 00:27:49.950
...but let's break it.

506
00:27:49.950 --> 00:27:51.050
Right! Let's do it!

507
00:27:51.050 --> 00:27:55.640
Usopp the brave warrior
of the sea is ready to fight!

508
00:27:57.980 --> 00:28:00.990
Hurry, will ya?
We're dying here!

509
00:28:02.800 --> 00:28:06.370
The scope of this planet's so vast and so grand

510
00:28:06.330 --> 00:28:09.720
That if treasure's out there, well where do you start?

511
00:28:09.670 --> 00:28:13.010
Keep your wits about you, don’t leave it to chance

512
00:28:13.030 --> 00:28:17.110
Yeah play it smart but don’t forget
that in the end you’re still rolling the dice

513
00:28:19.150 --> 00:28:20.280
And that's why...

514
00:28:23.020 --> 00:28:26.310
If someone gets in our way, well who cares?

515
00:28:26.360 --> 00:28:29.700
If someone’s running their mouth, well who cares?

516
00:28:29.680 --> 00:28:35.190
Let's sail out, yeah we'll tell all the losers here "bon voyage"

517
00:28:34.950 --> 00:28:36.880
Get lost and stay

518
00:28:36.640 --> 00:28:43.000
Cause even if you think what I'm doing
is dumb, I'm gonna get it done

519
00:28:43.010 --> 00:28:49.580
The more impossible the impressive, reach for the stars

520
00:28:49.690 --> 00:28:56.300
Yeah, even if you think what I'm doing
is dumb, I'm gonna take you on

521
00:28:56.330 --> 00:29:02.970
If we can sail across this vast sea we’ll find a paradise

522
00:29:03.320 --> 00:29:08.680
Go ahead and give it your best,
next time you look out your telescope

523
00:29:08.440 --> 00:29:10.480
You’ll find you’re one step closer
